# freebuff-proxy configuration — complete reference
#
# Every configuration key the proxy understands, with defaults. All keys can
# be set via environment variables, this .env file, or a JSON config file
# (config.example.json) — precedence: real environment > .env > JSON.
#
# For a ready-to-run SAFEST configuration, use .env.example instead — this
# file is the exhaustive reference (including optional/tuning keys).

# ── Mode (the only real decision) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated upstream token(s). EMPTY = bridge mode:
# the proxy stores no tokens; each client sends its own in
# Authorization: Bearer <token>. Pooled mode (tokens listed here) is best
# for one user with several accounts.
AUTH_TOKENS=

# With AUTH_TOKENS set, accept bridge-mode clients (their own token relayed)
# alongside the pool — hybrid mode. 0 = locked-down pooled-only instance.
#BRIDGE_ENABLED=true

# How long a bridge entry may sit unused before its runs are FINISHed and it
# is evicted from the cache (sliding TTL; zero or invalid → 72h).
#BRIDGE_IDLE_EVICT=72h

# ── Listening / access ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loopback by default — the proxy is only reachable from this machine.
# For a LAN/Docker container set LISTEN_ADDR=:3457 (all interfaces).
LISTEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:3457

# Protect the admin dashboard + POST /admin/reload. Defaults to factory
# password "123456" (a startup warning prompts rotation). Change it before
# exposing the port. Leave empty ONLY on loopback-only single-user installs.
ADMIN_TOKEN=123456
#
# Enable/disable the embedded admin dashboard at /admin. When false, all
# /admin routes return 404 and the dashboard struct is not created.
#DASHBOARD_ENABLED=true
#
# Show the Dev Tools page (batch chat, session spawner) in the admin
# dashboard. Default off: it is a manual testing surface that hammers /v1/*.
#DEVTOOLS_ENABLED=false

# Optional client auth for the OpenAI-compatible endpoint. When set, only
# requests bearing one of these keys (Authorization: Bearer or x-api-key)
# are served; leave empty to skip client auth. Overlaps with bridge mode —
# see README "API_KEYS × bridge" before combining.
#API_KEYS=

# Access-Control-Allow-Origin for /v1/* responses (default "*").
#CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN=*

# ── Upstream ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Upstream API base URL (default https://codebuff.com; the bare host is
# normalized to www.codebuff.com at load).
#UPSTREAM_BASE_URL=https://codebuff.com
# Upstream CLI version string, shown on the admin dashboard only
# (informational — no wire impact: the chat UA is pinned to
# ai-sdk/openai-compatible/1.0.0/codebuff, the ads UA to
# Freebuff-CLI/1.0.0, and session/auth endpoints to Bun/1.3.14; default 0.10.7).
#CLI_VERSION=

# ── Request translation tuneables (backend/internal/convert) ────────────────────
# These three are read DIRECTLY from the process environment (os.Getenv),
# not from -config JSON. In a native install, export them in your shell /
# systemd unit / launchd plist — the binary does NOT export .env values to
# process env. Under docker compose, .env is wired through `env_file` and
# IS exported to the container.
#
# COMPRESS_PROMPT (default OFF; 1/true/yes/on enables): compress long
# message lists before translation — middle user/assistant turns beyond a
# trailing budget (keep last 10) are replaced by ONE marker message, and
# content over 8 KiB on kept user/assistant turns is capped. Tool results,
# assistant tool_calls, system messages and the last message are never
# dropped or truncated (#58).
#COMPRESS_PROMPT=false
# CACHE_CONTROL_INJECTION (default ON; 0/false/off/no/disabled disables):
# add {"type":"ephemeral"} cache_control to every content block of the
# stable DeepSeek context prefix (messages at indices 2-3) when the block
# lacks one already, for prompt caching (#84).
#CACHE_CONTROL_INJECTION=true
# REASONING_IN_CONTENT (default OFF/empty): fold reasoning_content into
# delta.content as "<tag>...</tag>" text for legacy clients that never
# render a reasoning channel; the reasoning channel is preserved alongside
# and reasoning_details is never folded. true/1/on -> "think"; any other
# word becomes the tag (#44).
#REASONING_IN_CONTENT=false

# ── Account safety (anti-ban) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# SAFE_MODE=true applies the anti-ban preset when a knob is left unset:
# idle-run rotation 30m, request jitter 200ms. TLS is CLI-faithful
# (plain Go/Bun baseline, no browser JA3) — set TLS_FINGERPRINT=auto
# only for browser-evasion on datacenter IPs (e.g. SG). Keep this ON.
# Set SAFE_MODE=false only if you understand the tradeoffs.
#
# Egress impersonates the official upstream CLI: ads requests carry the
# Freebuff-CLI/1.0.0 User-Agent with a Chrome/124 body UA, chat requests the
# ai-sdk UA, and session/auth endpoints a plain Bun/1.3.14 — plus your real
# timezone/locale. TLS is plain Go (CLI baseline) unless overridden below.
SAFE_MODE=true

# TLS fingerprint for upstream egress: empty = plain Go/Bun baseline,
# CLI-faithful (default). Set to auto/chrome126/safari18/... only for
# browser JA3 evasion on datacenter IPs (SG).
#TLS_FINGERPRINT=

# Random delay in [0, REQUEST_JITTER) before each upstream chat call —
# makes egress look like a human, not a bot. 200ms under SAFE_MODE; 0 disables.
# For absolute lowest TTFB set REQUEST_JITTER=0 (instant) — 200ms keeps light
# anti-ban jitter while saving ~1.8s avg vs the old 2s.
REQUEST_JITTER=200ms

# Pause run rotation / session refresh after this idle period (upstream
# only sees activity while you actually use the proxy). 30m under SAFE_MODE;
# 0 disables.
IDLE_ROTATION_TIMEOUT=30m

# Max additional attempts after a transient transport failure (TLS/conn/EOF/
# timeout). Never retries 429/403/401. 1 = safe default; 0 disables.
TRANSIENT_RETRIES=1

# Negotiate HTTP/2 with the upstream (#51): real browsers advertise
# "h2,http/1.1", so forcing HTTP/1.1 at the TLS layer is a JA4 ALPN mismatch.
# false forces HTTP/1.1 (escape hatch for non-h2 upstreams).
#HTTP2_UPSTREAM=true

# Optional upstream account id: sent on every chat call as
# x-freebuff-acting-user-id. BAN RISK: the CLI sends the account's OWN id
# (derived from GET /api/v1/me), and the server honors the header only for
# the upstream web service account — any value other than the token's own
# account id impersonates another user. Only safe value: the token's own
# account id. (Pre-rename name USER_ID still works.) Leave empty to omit.
#ACTING_USER_ID=

# Make the proxy behave like the official CLI for a single account: with
# AUTH_TOKENS empty the token is sourced from
# ~/.config/manicode/credentials.json and every session manager adopts the
# CLI's ACTIVE session instance from freebuff-instance-owner.json; while the
# CLI process is alive a competing session is never created (issue #97).
#ADOPT_CLI_SESSION=false

# Fire the reference ad-chain + streak requests before the next session
# create after an upstream 428 waiting_room_required (issue #94(b), gated
# stub — best-effort, never blocks the request).
#WAITING_ROOM_CHAIN=false
# Streak maintenance (Account Maturity): one nightly run in the 60 minutes
# before the Pacific-midnight reset touches every account live (admit → one
# minimal turn → release; Auto = cheapest served unmetered row).
# Accounts with client traffic since the last Pacific reset are skipped.
# Default ON; set MATURITY_ENABLED=false to disable all automated touches.
#MATURITY_ENABLED=true
#MATURITY_TOUCH_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash
#MATURITY_TARGET_DAYS=7
# Quota auto-probe scheduler (ADR-0022): one session-less probe per token
# per Pacific day in the 2h window before its known quota reset. Default
# ON; set false to restore pre-scheduler behavior (manual probes only).
#QUOTA_AUTO_PROBE=true

# ── Timeouts & rotation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How often the token pool rotates to the next token (default 6h).
#ROTATION_INTERVAL=6h
# MASQ spill order: strict account index order (#1..#N) per model with
# per-(account, model) live-turn slots and a FIFO waiter queue.
# SLOTS_PER_ACCOUNT caps concurrent live turns per lane (default 2,
# 0 = unlimited). QUEUE_WAIT bounds one parked wait (default 30s);
# QUEUE_DEPTH caps parked waiters per lane (default 16, 0 = spill at
# once when full). A full queue or an elapsed wait spills silently to the
# next account, bounded by MAX_SPILL_ACCOUNTS (default 0 = unbounded).
# The end of the chain surfaces the existing 429 shape. All five apply
# live on reload. BUNKER: SLOTS_PER_ACCOUNT=1 - fully sequential turns.
#SLOTS_PER_ACCOUNT=2
#QUEUE_WAIT=30s
#QUEUE_DEPTH=16
#MAX_SPILL_ACCOUNTS=0
# Per-slot model pins (PIN_MODEL), e.g. "0:z-ai/glm-5.2;1:deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash".
# Requests for other models skip pinned slots (counted in metrics and shown
# on the Tokens page) without burning their quota or churning sessions.
# Slots without an entry serve any model. Empty = feature off. When every
# slot is pinned away from a model, requests fail fast naming the model.
# Applies live on reload; malformed values reject the config.
#PIN_MODEL=
# Per-request upstream timeout (default 15m).
#REQUEST_TIMEOUT=15m
# Per session-call (admission/poll/create) timeout (default 30s).
#SESSION_CALL_TIMEOUT=30s
# Registry (model catalog) refresh cadence (default 6h).
#REGISTRY_REFRESH=6h

# ── Model catalog ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated model allowlist: when set, only these RESOLVED model ids
# are served — /v1/models lists only them, and chat/messages/responses for
# any other model return 404 model_not_found. Empty = all models allowed.
#MODELS_ALLOW=
# true = /v1/models prunes models marked unavailable (region/tier/quota).
#MODELS_HIDE_UNAVAILABLE=false
#
# How long a model_unavailable admission refusal is remembered per model
# (off-window models short-circuit to the fallback within the TTL).
#MODEL_UNAVAILABLE_CACHE_TTL=1h

# ── Session lifecycle tuning ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Persist upstream session state to disk so a restart resumes an unexpired
# session instead of burning a fresh daily session slot. Opt-in: the session
# instance id + expiry AND the active agent runs (run id, agent, trace id)
# are written to SESSION_STATE_FILE (0600) keyed by a SHA-256 hash of your
# token — the raw token is never written. A restart adopts the persisted
# session + runs without re-creating them.
#SESSION_PERSIST=true
#SESSION_STATE_FILE=.freebuff-session-state.json
# Re-admit a session pre-emptively when less than this much time remains:
# the request rides the old session while the refresh runs in the
# background; the next request gets the fresh instance.
#SESSION_RE_ADMIT_LEAD=60s
# Reuse the last successful session state (skip redundant session poll GETs)
# within this window after a successful admission/poll.
#SESSION_PROBE_CACHE_TTL=15s

# ── Run lifecycle tuning ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bounded deferred-FINISH worker queue: rotated/drained runs are FINISHed
# by a background worker; when the queue is full the caller falls back to a
# synchronous FINISH bounded by RUN_FINISH_INLINE_TIMEOUT.
#RUN_FINISH_QUEUE_SIZE=64
#RUN_FINISH_INLINE_TIMEOUT=250ms
# Bound the draining-runs list: entries older than RUNS_DRAIN_TTL or beyond
# RUNS_DRAIN_QUEUE_CAP are force-dropped (their upstream FINISH is
# best-effort anyway).
#RUNS_DRAIN_QUEUE_CAP=64
#RUNS_DRAIN_TTL=10m

# ── Cost safety ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MUST stay "free": any other value routes requests as PAID and fresh free
# accounts get 402 "Out of credits". Do not change this.
COST_MODE=free

# ── Client Rate Limiting ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-source-IP token bucket rate limiter to prevent bursts, duplicate retries,
# and tool spam from hammering upstream. Requests exceeding the limit receive
# local HTTP 429 + Retry-After header immediately (zero upstream traffic).
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_IP: sustained requests/second per IP (0 = disabled; e.g. 20)
# RATE_LIMIT_BURST: maximum burst capacity (0 = defaults to 2 * RATE_LIMIT_PER_IP)
#RATE_LIMIT_PER_IP=0
#RATE_LIMIT_BURST=0

# ── CLI token auto-discovery ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# When AUTH_TOKENS is empty, the proxy reads credentials from the official
# CLI login files (~/.config/manicode|codebuff/credentials.json). That can
# silently flip bridge mode to pooled mode. NOTE: this knob is ENV-ONLY —
# it cannot be set in .env (it controls whether .env is read at all).
# Export it in your shell / systemd / compose environment to disable:
#   export AUTO_DISCOVER_TOKEN=false

# ── Observability ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Log level: debug | info | warn | error | trace (trace = wire-level bodies)
LOG_LEVEL=info
# Log format: text (key=value, colored) or json (one JSON object per line)
#LOG_FORMAT=text
# Optional log file (empty = stderr only). Paths are relative to the process
# working directory; the directory is created automatically.
#LOG_FILE=./logs/proxy.log
# One `access` line per HTTP request; false disables (healthz/metrics/OPTIONS
# are rate-limited to 1/min regardless)
#LOG_ACCESS=true
# Best-effort alert POSTs when the token pool is exhausted or a token is
# classified banned (issue #48; empty = disabled). At most one POST per
# event type per 5m; never blocks the request path.
#WEBHOOK_URL=
# Redact-and-dump upstream traffic to ./dump/ (debugging only)
#DEBUG_DUMP=false
